            <ArticleTitle>Assessment and treatment of pain in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Treating acute pain in the paediatric population poses challenges which include the lack of high levels of evidence and a universal pain measuring tool, contributing to the undertreatment of pain. A multimodal approach of topical and systemic analgesia, comfort measures and parental involvement remains the mainstay of pain management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
